# **1. Operative Creation**

## **1.1 Attributes**

Each operative has five attributes rated 0–3. Attributes drive all rolls and calculate vital statistics.

| **Attribute** | **Covers** |
| --- | --- |
| BODY | Physical strength, endurance, toughness. Drives melee attacks, physical feats, and raw resilience. |
| MIND | Reasoning, analysis, cognitive clarity. Drives deduction, problem-solving, and tactical thinking. |
| TECH | Technical proficiency, systems, and equipment. Drives hacking, engineering, medicine, and investigation. |
| AWARENESS | Perception, instinct, reading environments. Drives ranged attacks, detecting danger, and spatial judgment. |
| RESOLVE | Emotional stability, willpower, composure. Drives SPIKE resistance saves and social endurance. |

## **1.2 Attribute Generation**

### **Step 1 — Assign the Base Array**

Distribute the following five values across your five attributes in any order:

**  3  —  2  —  2  —  1  —  1**

### **Step 2 — Apply Specialisation Bonus**

Add +1 to any two different attributes currently rated 2 or lower. No single attribute may exceed 3.

### **Step 3 — Calculate Vitals**

**HP** = 10 + BODY     **COMPOSURE** = 5 + RESOLVE

## **1.3 Starting Skills**

Choose 3 skills at creation. All skills begin Untrained. Selected skills become Trained (+2).

Untrained: d10 + Attribute only. Trained: +2. Specialised (via advancement): +3.

## **1.4 Standard Issue Equipment**

All operatives receive the following at UGD HQ before deployment. No requisition required.

- UGD field uniform

- Subcutaneous SPIKE monitoring implant — reads own SPIKE level continuously; evaluates others at close range without a roll. Replaces handheld wand in the field.

- Flashlight

- Field radio

*Additional loadout items are requisitioned separately. See Section 9: Requisition Catalogue.*

# **2. Core Roll Protocol**

## **2.1 The Core Roll**

**d10 + ATTRIBUTE + SKILL  **≥  TARGET NUMBER (TN)

Apply a skill bonus only when clearly relevant. Untrained rolls use attribute alone.

## **2.2 Dice**

| **Die** | **When Used** |
| --- | --- |
| d10 | All controlled actions — combat attacks, skill checks, movement, technical tasks. |
| d20 | SPIKE and emotional rolls — instability saves, grounding attempts, behaviour table. |

## **2.3 Target Numbers**

| **TN** | **Difficulty** | **Typical Use** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 7 | Routine | No pressure; relevant skill; clear environment. |
| 9 | Standard | Default for most field actions and combat attacks. |
| 11 | Challenging | Time pressure, partial obstruction, unfamiliar situation. |
| 13 | Hard | Heavy cover, active interference, significant stakes. |
| 15 | Very Hard | Expert-level barrier, hostile environment, life-or-death. |
| 17 | Near-Impossible | Reserved for exceptional circumstances. |

## **2.4 Advantage and Disadvantage**

- Advantage: roll 2 dice of the relevant type; take the higher result.

- Disadvantage: roll 2 dice of the relevant type; take the lower result.

## **2.5 Critical Results (d10 only)**

| **Result** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- |
| Natural 10 — Critical Success | Combat: double base damage before adding weapon modifier. Non-combat: significant narrative bonus at GM discretion. |
| Natural 1 — Critical Fault | A complication arises — jam, noise, exposure, unintended consequence. Not an automatic total failure; something goes wrong. |

## **2.6 Rests**

| **Rest Type** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- |
| Short Rest | SPIKE −1. Roll Quick Recovery trait if applicable. |
| Long Rest | HP and COMPOSURE restored to maximum. SPIKE −2. Reaction pool fully restored. |

# **3. Combat Operations**

## **3.1 Initiative**

Roll **d10 + AWARENESS**. Act in descending order. Ties: player preference or GM call. Initiative is fixed for the encounter.

## **3.2 Turn Structure**

Each operative's turn consists of:

- 1 Action — attack, assist, use a skill, technical task, grounding attempt.

- 1 Minor Action — move 1 zone, draw a weapon, quick interaction.

*Actions and Minor Actions may be used in any order within the turn.*

## **3.3 Attack Resolution — Margin of Success**

One roll determines both hit and damage.

**d10 + ATTRIBUTE + SKILL  vs  ENEMY DEFENSE VALUE**

If the total meets or exceeds the enemy's Defense Value, the attack lands. The margin (total minus Defense Value) becomes base damage.

BASE DAMAGE   = roll total − Defense Value

FINAL DAMAGE  = base damage + weapon modifier − armour

- Natural 10: double the base damage before adding weapon modifier.

- Natural 1: miss regardless of modifiers; introduce a complication. Minimum 0 damage on any hit.

## **3.4 Engagement Zones**

| **Zone** | **Range Description** | **Typical Weapons** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| CLOSE | Melee range — direct contact. | Melee weapons; pistols at disadvantage. |
| NEAR | Pistol range. | Pistols, shotguns, SMGs. |
| FAR | Rifle range. | Rifles, carbines. |
| OUT OF REACH | Extreme distance. | Sniper rifles only. |

## **3.5 Movement**

| **Movement Type** | **Cost** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Standard | Minor Action | Move 1 zone. No additional cost. |
| Extended ×1 | Minor Action + −1 COMPOSURE | Move 2 zones. |
| Extended ×2 | Full Action | Move 2 zones. No COMPOSURE penalty. |

## **3.6 Weapons**

| **Class** | **Damage Modifier** | **Effective Range** | **Examples** | **Restriction** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Light | margin only (+0) | CLOSE / NEAR | Pistol, knife, baton. | — |
| Standard | margin +2 | NEAR / FAR | Rifle, carbine, SMG. | — |
| Heavy | margin +4 | FAR only | Sniper rifle, LMG. | Cannot move and attack on the same turn. |
| Shotgun | margin +4 | CLOSE / NEAR only | Combat shotgun. | Heavy class. Effective range NEAR or closer. Cannot move and attack same turn. |

*Shotgun is classified as Heavy (+4 damage) but is limited to CLOSE and NEAR range, unlike other Heavy weapons which operate at FAR.*

## **3.7 Armour**

| **Armour Class** | **Damage Reduction** | **Penalties** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Light | −2 final damage | — No penalties. |
| Medium | −4 final damage | −1 to all Mobility checks. |
| Heavy | −6 final damage | −1 to all Mobility checks. −1 to all AWARENESS checks. Extended movement costs +1 COMPOSURE instead of the standard rule. |

*Heavy armour imposes both a Mobility and an AWARENESS penalty. Operatives in heavy armour are slower and less perceptive.*

## **3.8 Reactions**

Each operative has 2 reactions per Long Rest. Reactions trigger outside your turn. They do not reset between encounters.

| **Reaction** | **Trigger / Requirement** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Overwatch | Must have used Aim as a Minor Action last turn. | Shoot any enemy who enters your line of sight. (Ranged only.) |
| Counterattack | You are attacked in melee. | Make an immediate return strike. (Melee only.) |
| Protect | An adjacent ally is targeted. | Interpose yourself — you take the hit instead. |
| Brace | You are targeted by any attack. | Reduce final damage from the triggering hit by 2. |

## **3.9 COMPOSURE Thresholds**

- COMPOSURE 1: −1 to all BODY checks.

- COMPOSURE 0: Immediate SPIKE Save (d20 + RESOLVE vs TN 14). All rolls suffer −1 until COMPOSURE is restored.

# **4. The SPIKE Scale**

SPIKE measures deviation from neurological Reset baseline. Rated 0–11. Rises in response to trauma, hostile environments, and SPIKE-inducing threats. Falls through rest and grounding. SPIKE is a medical condition — not a character flaw.

## **4.1 Scale Reference**

| **Level** | **Designation** | **Mechanical Effect** | **SPIKE Save** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 0 | SERENE | Baseline. No effect. The ideal operative state. | — |
| 1–2 | STABLE | No mechanical effect. Nominal baseline. | — |
| 3–5 | SHAKEN | −1 to all MIND rolls. | d20 + RESOLVE vs TN 9 when triggered. |
| 6–7 | CRACKED | −1 to MIND and RESOLVE. Hallucinations possible. | Save required when triggered. |
| 8–9 | OVERLOADED | Disadvantage on all social checks. Operative unreasonable in roleplay. | SPIKE Save required hourly. |
| 10 | SPIKED | Loss of character control. Roll Behaviour Table (d20) at turn start. | d20 + RESOLVE vs TN 16 at end of turn. Nat 20: SPIKE −2. Nat 1: SPIKE +1. |
| 11 | CONSUMED | 1d4 True Damage per turn until HP 0; then 1d4 RESOLVE damage per turn until 0. Death follows. | d20 + RESOLVE vs TN 18 at end of turn. Nat 1: damage rolls at Advantage. |

*True Damage at CONSUMED bypasses armour.*

## **4.2 Lowering SPIKE**

| **Method** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- |
| Short Rest | SPIKE −1. |
| Long Rest | SPIKE −2. |
| Grounding Action | Once per encounter. Action + d20 + MIND vs TN 13. Success: SPIKE −1. An ally at SPIKE 4 or lower may grant Advantage. |

## **4.3 Assisting a SPIKED Operative**

Requires an Action and meaningful roleplay (logic, routine, calm instruction).

**d20 + MIND  vs  TN 14**

| **Result** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- |
| Success | Target gains Advantage on their next SPIKE Save. |
| Failure | SPIKED operative lashes out — 1d4 damage to the helper. |
| Critical Failure | Both make RESOLVE Save vs TN 12. Target has Disadvantage on their next SPIKE Save. |

## **4.4 SPIKE Resonance**

When two characters’ SPIKE levels differ by 4 or more, the lower-SPIKE individual experiences instability in proximity. Both suffer Disadvantage on social checks while the gap persists. Log all resonance events on mission return.

## **4.5 Behaviour Table (SPIKE 10) — Roll d20 at start of each turn**

| **Roll** | **Behaviour** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | Shatter Point | Immediate SPIKE Save. Success: act normally. Fail: +1 SPIKE (risks CONSUMED). |
| 2 | Emotional Bleed | All CLOSE allies make SPIKE Save vs TN 14 or +1 SPIKE. −1 to all your rolls this turn. |
| 3 | Misplaced Trust | Latch onto nearest creature as ally regardless of reality. If they harm you: +1 SPIKE. |
| 4 | Violent Outburst | Attack nearest creature using full Action. If no target in range: move toward nearest. |
| 5 | Paranoid Break | All others treated as hostile until end of turn. Cannot benefit from Assist. |
| 6 | Panic Response | Use movement to flee perceived danger. Cannot move toward enemies. |
| 7 | Reckless Advance | Must move toward nearest threat. Advantage on next attack; all attacks against you have Advantage. |
| 8 | Disassociation | −2 to all rolls this turn. Cannot take Reactions. |
| 9 | Freeze | Lose Action. May take Minor Action only. |
| 10 | Collapse | Fall prone. Lose Action. Minor Action only. Gain +1 COMPOSURE at end of turn. |
| 11 | Sensory Overload | Disadvantage all rolls. Must reposition away from stimuli. If unable: −2 all rolls. |
| 12 | Erratic Action | Roll d10: 1–3 target wrong creature; 4–6 drop or mishandle item; 7–10 act normally. |
| 13 | Echo Loop | Repeat last meaningful action. If impossible: lose Action. |
| 14 | Target Lock | Advantage vs one chosen target; Disadvantage vs all others. Must pursue chosen target. |
| 15 | Compulsive Fixation | GM assigns fixation. Must focus on it this turn. +1 to related actions. |
| 16 | Emotional Surge | +2 to next attack roll. If the attack misses: +1 SPIKE. |
| 17 | Control Snap | SPIKE Save. Success: act normally. Fail: +1 SPIKE and −2 to all rolls this turn. |
| 18 | Hyper-Focus | GM defines one task. +2 to related rolls. Cannot take unrelated actions. |
| 19 | Moment of Clarity | Act normally this turn. SPIKE −1. |
| 20 | Fractured Clarity | Advantage on all rolls this turn. SPIKE −1 for this turn only, then resets. |

# **5. Skills**

Skills add +2 (Trained) or +3 (Specialised) to the relevant roll. Untrained: attribute only. Choose 3 at creation; additional skills gained through advancement.

| **Category** | **Skill** | **Attribute** | **Description** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| COMBAT | Firearms | AWARENESS | Guns, ranged attacks, aimed fire. |
| COMBAT | Close Combat | BODY | Brawling, melee, grappling. |
| PHYSICAL | Mobility | BODY | Running, climbing, dodging, parkour. |
| PHYSICAL | Stealth | AWARENESS | Sneaking, hiding, silent movement. |
| PHYSICAL | Survival | BODY | Tracking, navigation, scavenging. |
| TECHNICAL | Computing | TECH | Hacking, systems access, data retrieval. |
| TECHNICAL | Engineering | TECH | Repair, machinery, fabrication. |
| TECHNICAL | Medicine | TECH | First aid, trauma care, stabilisation. |
| MENTAL | Investigation | TECH | Clues, deduction, pattern recognition. |
| MENTAL | Awareness | AWARENESS | Noticing danger, reading environments, detecting concealment. |
| SOCIAL | Persuasion | MIND | Convincing, diplomacy, trust-building. |
| SOCIAL | Intimidation | MIND | Threats, dominance, coercion. |

*Investigation is driven by TECH (analysis, pattern recognition, memory). Awareness is driven by AWARENESS (environmental reading, instinct). These are distinct skills.*

*Note: the Awareness skill shares its name with the AWARENESS attribute. In play, context makes the distinction clear — the skill applies to active perception checks, the attribute is the stat rolled.*

# **6. Traits**

Traits are passive abilities gained at milestones. Characters begin with none. Maximum 6 traits per operative. No trait may be taken twice.

## **6.1 Combat Traits**

| **Trait** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- |
| Steady Aim | Ignore movement penalties when making ranged attacks. |
| Close Quarters Fighter | +1 to Close Combat rolls at CLOSE range. |
| Quick Draw | Drawing a weapon costs no Minor Action. |
| Combat Instinct | +1 to all Initiative rolls. |
| Suppressive Fire | On a successful Firearms attack, the target suffers −1 to their next roll. |
| Relentless | Downing an enemy grants +1 to your next action. |
| Last Stand | At 0 HP (not yet dead): +1 to all rolls until stabilised. |

## **6.2 Mental Traits**

| **Trait** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- |
| Pattern Recognition | +1 to Investigation when analysing repeating clues. |
| Cold Reader | +1 to detect lies or hidden intent. |
| Focused Mind | +1 to SPIKE Saves per scene. |
| Rapid Analysis | Once per encounter, ask the GM one tactical question for a truthful hint. |
| Memory Recall | Automatically remember all previously encountered details. |
| Problem Solver | +1 to TECH or MIND rolls when under time pressure. |
| Unshakable Logic | Advantage on checks to resist paranoia or hallucinations. |

## **6.3 Social Traits**

| **Trait** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- |
| Silver Tongue | +1 to Persuasion in calm, non-hostile situations. |
| Intimidating Presence | +1 to Intimidation when asserting dominance. |
| Disarming | First social interaction in a scene ignores hostility penalty. |
| Trust Builder | Allies gain +1 to their first roll after you assist them. |
| Commanding Voice | Once per encounter, one Persuasion or Intimidation roll affects multiple targets. |

## **6.4 Physical Traits**

| **Trait** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- |
| Agile | +1 to all Mobility checks. |
| Silent Steps | +1 to Stealth when not in direct line of sight. |
| Endurance | +2 to maximum HP. |
| Quick Recovery | Roll +1d6 additional HP during a Short Rest. Once per day. |
| Sure Footing | Ignore difficult terrain penalties. |
| Climber | Advantage on all climbing or vertical movement checks. |
| Sprint Burst | Once per encounter, move +1 extra zone for free. |

## **6.5 Technical Traits**

| **Trait** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- |
| Hacker's Edge | +1 to Computing when actively breaching systems. |
| Field Engineer | Repair simple devices without tools. |
| Jury Rig | Once per session, temporarily repair a broken item. |
| Efficient Operator | Reduce time required for technical actions by half. |
| Drone Familiarity | +1 when interacting with or controlling drone units. |
| Systems Insight | Ask one question about any device or system per scene. |
| Backup Plan | Once per session, declare you prepared for a situation (GM approval required). |

# **7. Emotional Flaws**

Emotional Flaws are narrative scars acquired through play when a character suffers extreme trauma. Roleplay-first: they shape how an operative carries what they have been through. The examples below are a starting list; GM and player may define others.

## **7.1 Triggering a Flaw**

| **Option** | **Mechanic** | **Reward / Cost** |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Lean In | Act according to the flaw's impulse. | +1 to the roll OR +1 COMPOSURE. |
| Resist | d10 + RESOLVE vs TN 9. Success: act normally. Failure: −1 to roll or +1 SPIKE (GM choice). | Nothing on success. Penalty on failure. |

## **7.2 Flaw Reference**

| **Flaw** | **Trigger** | **Effect** | **Lean-In Benefit** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Fear of Attachment | Forming or relying on close bonds. | −1 to social rolls involving trust. | +1 when acting independently. |
| Bottled Rage | Frustration, disrespect, loss of control. | Risk of aggressive response. | +1 to Close Combat. |
| Emotional Numbness | High-stress or emotional situations. | −1 to social connection rolls. | Immune to first COMPOSURE loss per scene. |
| Paranoia | Uncertainty, hidden information. | Difficulty trusting others. | +1 to Awareness checks. |
| Survivor's Guilt | Others being harmed or at risk. | Hesitation or self-sacrifice pressure. | +1 when actively protecting others. |
| Control Fixation | Chaotic or unpredictable situations. | Must attempt to control outcomes. | +1 to planning or preparation actions. |

# **8. Advancement**

## **8.1 Milestone Progression**

Advancement is milestone-based. The GM signals when the party reaches one. At each milestone, the operative chooses one:

| **Option** | **Effect** |
| --- | --- |
| Gain a New Skill | Add any untrained skill at Trained level (+2). |
| Specialise a Skill | Upgrade a Trained skill (+2) to Specialised (+3). |
| Gain a Trait | Select any trait from Section 6. Maximum 6 traits per operative. |
| Increase Max COMPOSURE | +1 to maximum COMPOSURE. Subject to GM-set campaign cap. |
| Reduce an Emotional Flaw | Rare. Requires meaningful narrative resolution across multiple sessions and explicit GM approval. |

## **8.2 Other Progression**

- Knowledge — what the party uncovers stays with them. Information is currency.

- Access — credentials, clearance codes, and bypassed security open doors force cannot.

- Equipment — better tools recovered in the field or requisitioned from the Directorate.

- Allies — contacts who owe the team something may be worth more than any weapon.

# **9. Requisition Catalogue**

Before departing UGD HQ, operatives may requisition field loadout items from the catalogue below. Record all selections on the Operative Dossier (Doc 14-C) and export the JSON file to your GM to log equipment to the UGD Mainframe.

## **9.1 Weapons**

Select up to 2 weapons. Record weapon name, class, range, and any notes on the Operative Dossier.

| **Class** | **Weapons** | **Damage Modifier** | **Effective Range** | **Notes** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Light | Pistol, Knife | margin only (+0) | CLOSE / NEAR | Concealable, fast, mobile. Best suited for speed and concealment over stopping power. |
| Standard | Rifle | margin +2 | NEAR / FAR | Reliable operational weapon. Balanced between mobility and lethality. |
| Heavy | Sniper Rifle, LMG | margin +4 | FAR only | Slow, high-impact. Cannot move and attack on the same turn. |
| Shotgun | Combat Shotgun | margin +4 | CLOSE / NEAR only | Heavy class. High stopping power at close range. Cannot move and attack on the same turn. |

## **9.2 Armour**

Select one armour type, or none. Record armour type and armour value on the Operative Dossier.

| **Class** | **Damage Reduction** | **Penalties** | **Description** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Light | −2 final damage | None. | Soft-plate concealed armour. No mobility or awareness penalties. |
| Medium | −4 final damage | −1 to Mobility checks. | Tactical hard-plate carrier. Imposes encumbrance penalty to movement. |
| Heavy | −6 final damage | −1 to Mobility checks. −1 to AWARENESS checks. Extended movement costs +1 COMPOSURE. | Full tactical rig. Maximum protection; significant mobility and perception penalties. |

## **9.3 Field Equipment**

Select up to 3 additional items. Record on the Operative Dossier under Additional Equipment.

| **Item** | **Action Cost** | **Effect** | **Uses** |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Medkit | Action | Roll d10 + BODY. The result is the number of HP restored to the target. | Single use per kit. |
| Bandages | Minor Action | Stabilise a downed operative (brings them to 1 HP). Does not restore HP beyond stabilisation. No roll required. | Single use. |
| Hacking Kit | — (required) | Required for all Computing checks against secured electronic systems, terminals, and locked doors. Without a kit, such checks cannot be attempted. | Unlimited. Consumed only on GM discretion for extreme use. |
| Flashbang | Action | All targets in CLOSE range must make d10 + AWARENESS vs TN 11 or suffer Disadvantage on all rolls until the end of their next turn. | Single use. |
| Breach Charge | Action to place; Minor Action to detonate | Destroys a standard door, wall section, or lock. Can be set on a delay. | Single use. |
| Handcuffs | Action (on incapacitated or willing target) | Restrained target cannot take physical actions. Requires successful Close Combat check vs TN 9 to apply. | Reusable. |
| SPIKE Wand | Minor Action | Reads the SPIKE level of a target at CLOSE or NEAR range. Supplements the operative's subcutaneous implant for evaluating others when close-range implant scan is insufficient. | Unlimited. |

*The subcutaneous SPIKE implant issued to all operatives reads the operative**'**s own level continuously. The SPIKE Wand is for field evaluation of others, not self-monitoring.*

*Medkit and Bandages serve different functions: Medkit restores HP; Bandages only stabilise (1 HP). Carry both for full trauma coverage.*

